UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'SHOULD AN INSTRUMENT FOR ENGLAND ONLY BE REPRESENTABLE BELOW UK? OWNER VOCABULARY DECISION. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. UK Approved Document M volume 2 (REF-00992) says on its first pages that it is for use in England. Rows from it carry jurisdiction UK, the only spelling jurisdiction-philosophy.md section 3.3 allows, which has no sub-national code. Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland have their own accessibility regulations, so a UK row reads as a claim about all four. Adversarial finding 160 (WITHHELD-FOR-OWNER). RESOLVE: owner rules whether a sub-national code or a scope note is wanted; if yes, a vocabulary change in a tooling PR, then a re-filing of REF-00992 rows by new rows. DERIVE: select count(*) from source_value_extractions where ref_id = ''REF-00992'' and jurisdiction = ''UK''; grep -n ''For use in England'' retrieval-log/session_2026-10-30-rest-landing-parameter/0e5d4dee25b341f4-full-text.txt. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. Wider than England: REF-00995 (Flemish decree, BE), REF-01013 (Ontario, CA) and REF-01029 (Madrid, ES) also carry a national code for a sub-national instrument; JurisdictionCode has no sub-national member. Owner question 5: sub-national code (vocabulary and bucket changes, re-filing) or a scope note (no tooling).', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-077';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'PARAMETERS 7 AND 10 HOLD NO EXTRACTION AFTER FOUR SOURCES WERE READ AGAINST THE WHOLE CATALOGUE, AND PARAMETERS 5 AND 8 REST ON FEW. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Neither of the code sources, the Spanish order, the Korean annex, the Portuguese pages nor the Anthropometry report holds a reverberation time or colour temperature figure (their scans say so, with the sweeps used). Room acoustics and lighting codes are not among the held sources. The parameters exist, with no direction set, so a batch that reads a room-acoustics or lighting code is the only way they get a row. Parameter 8 (LRV contrast) has one numeric source (UK Approved Document M para 0.26) and two absence rows. RESOLVE: a research batch aimed at room acoustic and lighting standards (for example the Irish TGD, DIN 18041, BS 8300, EN 12464), logged search first. DERIVE: select parameter_id, count(*), count(distinct ref_id) from source_value_extractions group by 1. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. CORRECTION: the proposed remedy (fetch the Irish TGD M 2022) contradicts OR-16 (read what we hold first) and names a source already held (REF-01018, with REF-01015 and REF-01014). Derive the unread: select parameter_id, status, count(*) from v_scan_ledger where parameter_id in (7, 10) group by 1, 2. Resolve by full-read scans of held sources first; the batch-01 acoustic stash leads need --verify-authors if re-admitted (that batch''s co-authors were fabricated).', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-078';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'NO CO-1 SOURCE HAS BEEN RETRIEVED FOR DOOR, CORRIDOR OR TURNING-SPACE DIMENSIONS. R1 PASSES ONLY BECAUSE A SEARCH WAS TARGETED AT CO-1. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Execution 198 (PubMed, three AND-ed concept groups) and execution 201 (a web search in long natural language) were aimed at disabled-persons-organisation or lived-experience dimension guidance and returned none; 198 was a query-shape failure (its diagnosis was corrected after execution 200 returned on-topic work), 201 returned code and housing-authority pages and itself said a targeted search was needed. The DoD R1 line reads PASS on a targeted search with no source. RESOLVE: a targeted retrieval at Disability Rights UK, Scope, the Centre for Accessible Environments, the Centre for Excellence in Universal Design, Disabled People''s Organisations International and national wheelchair-user organisations, with the Co-1 provenance rules of governance/co1-operational.md; log each query first. DERIVE: select exec_id, target_evidence_type, results_admitted from search_executions where target_evidence_type = ''co1'' and created_by_session like ''session_2026-11-06%''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). CONFIRMED. Same structure as GAP-049 (R1 passes on a targeted search with no source). Research PR after the read-first scans.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-079';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'SIX PRIMARY-STUDY CANDIDATES ARE STAGED ON ABSTRACTS AND NONE HAS A REACHABLE FULL TEXT; THE CROSS-FILING ID OF ONE IS UNSETTLED. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Candidates 150 (Koontz 2010), 151 (Steinfeld 2010 review), 152 (King 2011), 153 (Higuchi 2009), 154 (Paquet 2012), 155 (Savelsbergh 1998) are PENDING-VERIFICATION. Europe PMC reports no open full text for Koontz and Steinfeld; the others were not tried. Admission cross-files to the stash ids where the DOI is held: REF-00784 (Koontz), REF-00972 (King), REF-00982 (Paquet), all RETIRED. Candidate 151''s DOI (10.1080/10400430903520280, PubMed) sits on two unrelated pre-reset stash rows (REF-00059, REF-00192: the GAP-008 shuffled-DOI defect), while REF-00044 carries the review''s exact title with a different DOI (10.1080/10400430903496580); which DOI is right is unverified. Tier guesses are 3 for Koontz, King, Higuchi, Paquet and Savelsbergh and 2 for Steinfeld, corrected after the pass; Koontz and Steinfeld share an author (Feathers), so an admission of both needs an independence check against full text. Koontz states, in its abstract, that between 10% and 100% of users could not manoeuvre in spaces meeting the US guideline (harm, R7). RESOLVE: obtain full texts through a library route (owner), then admit each through the pipeline, reusing the stash id; settle REF-00044 against Crossref first. DERIVE: select candidate_id, title, disposition from search_candidates where candidate_id between 150 and 155. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. The typed tier_guess columns still read 1 on candidates 150 and 152 beside notes saying 3 (see the new gap on typed columns). The REF-00044 DOI question is answerable from held payloads: PubMed and a Crossref reference list both give 10.1080/10400430903520280, which sits on REF-00059 and REF-00192, so add-source would refuse an admission under R9 until GAP-008/GAP-030 land. Owner question 7 (library route).', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-080';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'CITATION MINING OF THE ANTHROPOMETRY REPORT IS DEFERRED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. R2 obliges mining of a tier 1 to 3 anchor. The report (REF-00468) cites the Canadian UDI wheelchair study and the BS 8300 research it compares against, and the 2010 follow-ups. Its bibliography begins at PDF page 170 (report page 159), not 159 as the deferral note says; evidence_sources.pages is the PDF count (173) against a report pagination that ends at 162. Forward mining needs a citation index not queried. The deferral is assigned to the next batch by the GAP-025 mechanism. RESOLVE: run a backward pass over the persisted bibliography and a forward pass, log both with log-mining --notes. DERIVE: select slug, local_ref_id, backward, forward, deferred_reason from citation_mining where local_ref_id = ''AWM-01''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). CONFIRMED. The citation_mining deferral row still states the wrong page range (159-173; the bibliography is from PDF page 170) and carries backward = 1, forward = 1 on a deferral (GAP-021 behaviour, decided by GAP-022). Research PR.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-081';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'FIGURES STATED IN THE SOURCES READ AND LEFT UNFILED, AND CONCEPTS THE REPORT NAMES THAT NO OBSERVATION RECORDS. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Left unfiled by choice or for want of a quotable sentence, each stated in a persisted payload: the Anthropometry report''s percentile tables (cell sequences with no row labels in the extracted text), its 210 cm width for 95 percent of scooter users at the 180-degree turn (the sentence straddles a page break), its clear floor area, knee and toe clearance, latch-side clearance and grip-force concepts (no observation was harvested for them); the Spanish order''s 1,50 m circles at play areas, lift cabins, tables, kiosks and fountains (arts 8, 27 and others), its articles 6, 7 and 14 free heights; the Korean annex''s lift-front 1.4 m by 1.4 m, the 0.9 m ramp-width relaxation, competition-wheelchair figures (1.2 m door, 1.5 m by 1.5 m turning) and 1.5 m by 1.5 m passing zones; the Portuguese lift door 0,8 m and ramp exceptions; the UK 1500 by 1500 mm landing (2.7(d)) and manoeuvring space (3.28(a)), not filed on parameter 5 because the text calls them a landing and a manoeuvring space; the ADA passing spaces (403.5.3). RESOLVE: a catalogue re-reading with a derived figure inventory (see the SW gap on the scan procedure), then rows or declinations. DERIVE: the scan notes of source_scans for these refs list each one: select ref_id, notes from source_scans where created_by_session like ''session_2026-11-06%''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. CORRECTION: the reason given for not filing the 210 cm figure is false, the sentence is whole on PDF page 167 (the report repeats the long description there). O