UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'THE PORTUGUESE DECREE IS HELD AS 5 OF 20 PAGES, AND ITS TURNING DIMENSION IS NOT AMONG THEM. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. REF-01032 (Decreto-Lei 163/2006) text covers pages 1, 2, 9, 10 and 20 of 20. Items 2.2.1, 2.2.2 and 2.3.3 require a manoeuvre zone for a 360-degree rotation but the dimension sits in section 4.4, which is not held, so parameter 5 has no Portuguese row. REF-01026 is an unverified duplicate of the same decree. Parameters 7, 8, 10 and 11 are NOT examined for it. RESOLVE: retrieve the whole Diario da Republica issue (the persisted retrieval was partial), derive its full text with scripts/research/full_text.py, re-read; supersede or verify REF-01026. DERIVE: select ref_id, text_scope, pages_read, pages_total from source_scans where ref_id in (''REF-01032'',''REF-01026''). || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). CONFIRMED. Research PR: retrieve the whole issue, derive its full text, supersede REF-01026.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-083';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'WHETHER THE UK 1500 BY 1500 mm LANDING AND MANOEUVRING SPACES ARE TURNING SPACES IS NOT SETTLED BY ANY HELD SOURCE. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. UK Approved Document M volume 2 states 1500 x 1500 mm for the level landing before an entrance (2.7(d)) and the manoeuvring space before a lifting device (3.28(a)), and refers detail to BS 8300, which is not held. The wheelchair turning space of its sanitary guidance is carried by a diagram that was not read. Parameter 5 therefore has US (ADA 304.3.1, 1525 mm), Singapore, Spanish, Korean and report rows and no UK row. RESOLVE: obtain BS 8300 text, or read the diagrams of Approved Document M as page images (scripts/research/page_image.py), then file or decline. DERIVE: select jurisdiction, claimed_value, claimed_unit from source_value_extractions where parameter_id = 5 order by jurisdiction. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). CONFIRMED. Depends on owner question 7 (BS 8300) or reading the Approved Document diagrams as page images.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-084';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'EVERY READING RECORDED IN THESE TWO BATCHES IS pre-screen; NO SOURCE WAS READ END TO END AND NO OPEN PASS WAS DONE. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. All scan rows are method pre-screen with open_pass_done 0: located by keyword and clause number, a handful of pages read in full each. Each batch''s first scans then asserted absences that the critic disproved from the same payloads (door width and operating force in the Anthropometry report; a 22 N control force on a held Portuguese page; headroom and turning values in the UK text), so every ''no value found'' sentence in a pre-screen scan note is unverified. The rows and notes now carry the corrections, but the same sources have not been read in full. RESOLVE: full-read scans with the open pass (quantities the catalogue lacks) for REF-00468, REF-00992, REF-00987, REF-01028, REF-01031; treat any absence statement in an existing scan note as a lead. DERIVE: select ref_id, method, open_pass_done, count(*) from source_scans group by 1, 2, 3. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY, UNDERSTATED. Root cause: v_scan_ledger gives READ-NOTHING-FOUND whenever text_scope = ''full'', whatever the method (verified by the author: select status, method, count(*) from v_scan_ledger group by 1, 2), so pre-screens count as read and scan_debt fell on readings later disproved. See the new gap on the ledger. Closed by one predicate there.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-085';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'THE DEFINITION-OF-DONE GATE READS NEITHER source_scans NOR source_value_extractions, SO COMPLIANT SAYS NOTHING ABOUT THE EXTRACTION ROWS. TOOLING PR (rule 10). Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Re-run research_batch_dod.py --session on either session: R5 and R11 print EXAMINED: 0, R16-scan examines one admission, and no rule reads the extraction or scan tables, so the figures a determination rests on are checked only by db.py''s write-time verbatim test (which cannot see a column assignment, a locator, a unit or a role). Adversarial findings 153 and 166. RESOLVE: add the smallest rules that bind to a falsifiable property of those rows: claim_text verbatim against the persisted artefact at gate time; loc_note and source_section present; unit in the parameter''s family; a condition row has its edge; and an absence statement in a scan note cites its sweep. Each must print EXAMINED and fail on a seeded defect (selftest). DERIVE: python3 scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py --session session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 | grep -c ''EXAMINED: 0''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. CORRECTION: R16-scan does read source_scans; three registered checks read source_value_extractions; one of the five proposed rules already exists (extraction_relations_integrity). The residual is a gate-time claim_text re-verification. Smallest design: walk claim_text in observation_verbatim_audit.py with the same locate_quote (about 20 lines, REUSE), or close as accepted because the capture path never hand-writes rows.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-086';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'NO SANCTIONED WRITER CORRECTS A LENS, A LOCATOR, A SETTING, THE contested FLAG, A CANDIDATE''S harm_finding OR TITLE, OR A SCAN NOTE. TOOLING PR (rule 10). Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. amend-extraction takes comparator, extraction_method, extraction_status, figure_role, root_ref_id and root_type; given a same-value it only appends the reason to notes. So a wrong locator (extraction 211: item 8 for item 13), a wrong setting (193: whole sample of 495, the task sample is 339), an inconsistent lens (see the lens DEC gap) and an unraised contested on the ADA 1525 mm rows (183, 193) can only be corrected in notes, and a corrected scan is a new scan row. amend-search raises harm_finding on a search but nothing raises it on a candidate (150 carries harm 0 beside search 197 raised). Candidate 151''s title reads D Souza for D''Souza. RESOLVE: one writer, ''correct-extraction'', that rewrites a named non-key column recording the replaced value (as amend-source does), and amend verbs for candidate harm_finding and title. DERIVE: python3 scripts/db.py amend-extraction --help | grep -A1 -- --field. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. Locator and section widening is real (add loc_* and source_section to the amendable set, about 2 lines); setting, value and unit are already ruled (OR-3, workplan T-1b step 8); lens re-key is gated by OR-1c; the candidate harm_finding and title parts re-open GAP-059 (CLOSED-DECIDED); contested has no reader (no view reads it, verified by the author), so the sound move is to delete the --contested writer flag, not to build an amender. Owner question 8 for in-place locator correction.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29