UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'update-locator REWRITES created_by_session AND created_at ON A STASH ROW ALTHOUGH ITS DOCSTRING SAYS ONLY THE STATUS MOVES. TOOLING PR (rule 10). Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Marking the REF-00468 lead PROMOTED set the row''s created_by_session to the batch session and created_at to today, on a row whose notes say it was migrated on 2026-08-23. The code comments call this ''who worked this lead'' by design; the docstring and the column names say otherwise, so a reader will take the row for one created in this batch. Adversarial finding 178 of the first pass notes it. RESOLVE: add updated_by_session / updated_at to source_locators, or stop rewriting the created_* pair. DERIVE: select ref_id, status, created_by_session, created_at, notes from source_locators where ref_id = ''REF-00468''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. Code behaviour confirmed, but the overwritten created_* values were NULL on that row, so nothing was lost, and pass 8 finding 184 survived it as designed. Close as accepted.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-093';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'ROWS IN METRES, CENTIMETRES, MILLIMETRES AND NEWTONS ARE FILED BESIDE ONE ANOTHER ON PARAMETERS 4, 6, 9 AND 11, AND THE ENGINE OWNS NO LENGTH OR FORCE FAMILY. See GAP-072, which this extends. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. Each row keeps the unit its source states (1,80 m, 80 cm, 915 mm, 22.2 N, 5 lbf given with its newton equivalent), so compose_value over any of these parameters returns NULL with ''stated in different units'' as soon as two sources differ, exactly as on parameter 12. Only the gradient family exists. RESOLVE: add a length family (m, cm, mm) and a force family (N), derived from the unit table not listed in code; then re-run the determination for parameters 4, 6, 9, 11. DERIVE: select parameter_id, claimed_unit, count(*) from source_value_extractions where parameter_id in (4, 6, 9, 11) group by 1, 2. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. Duplicate of GAP-072 and of ruled workplan T-1b step 9 (OR-10). CORRECTION: the force half is wrong, parameter 6 holds only N (select claimed_unit, count(*) from source_value_extractions where parameter_id = 6 group by 1). Build the ruled length family; no force family.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-094';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'PREFLIGHT PRINTS ADVISORY FAILURES THAT NO SESSION HAS DIAGNOSED, AND TWO TESTS ARE RED ON UNTOUCHED main. Found in sessions session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2 (PRs 211 and 212); the adversarial findings are in adversarial_findings, passes 8 and 9. scripts/tests/test_scan_contract.py cases G01 (R16-scan grandfathers an old batch and fails a new admission with no catalogue reading) and G02 (a targeted reading does not discharge R16-scan) fail on origin/main as well as here (checked in a worktree of origin/main). The other six advisory checks print FAIL on this branch in both PRs; they were not run against origin/main, so whether any is new is UNVERIFIED. An advisory failure that is always red teaches the reader to ignore all of them. RESOLVE: run each on a worktree of origin/main, record which are red there, fix or retire each (deletion needs only evidence, CLAUDE.md section 8). DERIVE: scripts/preflight.sh 2>&1 | grep -E ''^\[FAIL\]''; python3 scripts/tests/test_scan_contract.py | grep -E ''\[✗\]''. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. G01 and G02 fail because the test picks the most recent admitting session, which is now after R16_SCAN_FROM (scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py); fix is a fixture edit of about two lines. All six advisory checks are red on origin/main as well, so none is new; scan_debt is red by design. Close the six as known debt.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-095';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'ADVERSARIAL PASS 7 IS STILL OPEN, AND ITS CLOSING NEEDS THE OWNER OR A TOOLING CHANGE. Carried from the previous session so that it is on the registry; not caused by these batches. close-adversarial-pass refuses pass 7 because finding 140 names a migration path the rebuild deleted. RESOLVE: owner decides whether to dispose finding 140 OWNER-RULED or a tool allows a deleted-artefact disposition; then close. DERIVE: select pass_id, closed_at from adversarial_passes where closed_at is null. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: RESOLUTION ANALYSIS (Opus, read-only, 2026-11-06; scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2/resolution-analysis-GAP-074-096.md, section for this gap). PARTLY. CORRECTION: four passes are open, not one (verified by the author: select pass_id, closed_at from adversarial_passes where closed_at is null gives 1, 2, 5, 7). Passes 1 and 2 are held open by ruling; pass 5 has undisposed sustained findings (new gap). Disposing finding 140 cannot unblock pass 7: closing checks only that the artefacts of SURVIVED findings resolve. Owner question 6.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:29' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-096';
